{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546020-alternative-week-of-nightmares","id":1546020,"title":"Alternative Week of nightmares","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-17T01:59:38-08:00","id":1546020,"title":"Alternative Week of nightmares","content":"So I've found a neat alternative Week of nightmares on another forum where instead of Ravnos three other Three Antediluvians awaken, Brujah, Ventrue, and Lasombra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This tied to a simple idea. An Alternate Week of Nightmares. Instead of Ravnos, Three Antediluvians awaken, Brujah, Ventrue, and Lasombra.<br /> The first thing anyone knows about it is Ventrue standing in front of Palazzo Montecitorio in Rome, at Noon because he has Fortitude 10 and can do that, and declaring himself King of Kings.<br /> <br /> By the time the week is over, the three Antediluvians might be dead, or might not be, but at least have been driven into hiding. Three clans have been devestated. The Sabbat, the Anarchs, and the Camarilla have all suffered heavy loses. The Inner Circle has secret talks with the Black Hand and the two Sects officially merge. The Laws imposed by Ventrue during his short reign as King of Earth remain in effect, drastically changing the way kindred and kine both live their lives.<br /> <br /> In this setting, the Sabbat, the Camarilla, and the Anarchs form a political tripod, pulling and pushing against each other. There is no more war between the sects. The Sabbat's more monsterous practices are grudgingly accepted by the other two factions. They have no other choice in the matter. They all suffered heavy loses and none would survive alone. </div> </div> </div>TL;DR It starts with Ventrue standing in front of Palazzo Montecitorio in Rome declearing him self the king of kings and ends with all three of the Antediluvians committing a mutual kill or at least slnking off into shadows and the The Sabbat, the Anarchs, and the Camarilla getting forming a allance. Partly due to wanting to recover the devastation such the event and partly because Ventrue put a geass on all the vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dominate 10: Lawgiver</b><br /> <br /> The King's word is law. This is how it always has been and how it always should be. And any law that can be broken is no law at all. The Ventrue Antediluvian knows both these truths very well and has endeavored to embody them. Using this power, the King's decrees become universal law. They cannot be disobeyed. The Law binds everyone, universally, without exception. Ignorance is no protection.<br /> <br /> System: The Law is not a trifling thing. It is the foundation of society. As such, this power cannot be used lightly. For the King's decrees to become Laws there must be pomp, procedure, circumstance and ceremony. The King must stand before an assembled audience and officially declare that he is making a law. He announces what the new Law is, then spends some number of blood points to seal it. The more extreme the Law, the more blood points it costs. The Law must be universally applicable. It cannot single anyone out or carve out exceptions for some people. A law that only applies to some isn't a law at all. Once the law has been announced and sealed with blood, it must be sent to all the corners of the Earth. In previous ages, this would have been accomplished by messengers on sailing ships. Today, the internet works just fine, as does worldwide television broadcasts.<br /> <br /> Once the King declares and seals a Law and it is sent to all the corners of the Earth, no mortal or vampire of lesser generation can disobey it. Most other supernatural creatures and Antediluvian vampires may attempt to disobey it, but this requires a Difficulty 9 Willpower Test.<br /> <br /> Mummies have an easier and harder time of it. They can safely ignore any such Law that violates Maat. A law that causes strife is no law at all. However, they must obey all Laws that are in accordance with Maat, and attempting to break one has the same consequences as intentionally breaking Maat.<br /> <br /> Laws declared by this power remain binding even after the King's death. Only a King using this power can overturn a Law imposed by this power.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Honstly besides making for a good contrast of By nights studio version of WtA (and by extension WtE) where the garou nation split due to political differences. It make you think about other alternative Week of Nightmares where other Antediluvians awaken...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T04:53:22-08:00","id":1546023,"title":"","content":"I've always been a fan of the VtM: Bloodlines scenario, the end time of the eldest being awake and active has come and no one really noticed much of a difference. Such a stagnant &quot;end times&quot; feels more appropriate for vampires who by their very nature are unchanging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T01:33:39-08:00","id":1546065,"title":"","content":"There were periods when more than one Antediluvian was awake and around yet the world quietly not ended<br /> Between Erik Eigermann's around 600 BC Embrace and Alexander of Paris&quot;s around 700 BC Embrace, the last confirmed thing the Ventrue Antediluvian was active and Embraced (quite a feat for someone who was dead...), 260 BC when Arikel advised Prince Alchias of Syracuse and the Dark Ages (adding the 33 AD date when Sutekh went missing and he last time anyone has seen Haqim was in the British Isles in 121 CE, where he was engaged in philosophical conversations with the Ventrue Prince of London, Mithras) when Cappadocius, the Lasombra Antediluvian, the Eldest and Saulot (and if you accept the Tale of the Twin Gods and the Tale of the Tiger Queen and the Spider King both Zapatashura and Ennoia were active and had a nice quarell with the Kuei-Jin) <br /> (Arikel and Absimilliard were basically wake the whole time and the Eldest not really slumbered quietly either - Malkav is a wild card with his Madness Network status is)<br /> And the world is... well not ended. Nor the Clans went extinct<br /> The ennui and stagnant end times a bit more terrifying then the Age of the Returned Blood Gods<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T03:55:51-08:00","id":1546072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546020-alternative-week-of-nightmares?p=1546023#post1546023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always been a fan of the VtM: Bloodlines scenario, the end time of the eldest being awake and active has come and no one really noticed much of a difference. Such a stagnant &quot;end times&quot; feels more appropriate for vampires who by their very nature are unchanging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Odd fact: I used Wormwood as the basis for a switch from V:TM to Requiem.<br /> <br /> In 2001, God sent his Red Star to smite the Kindred and 90% of them including the Antediluvians all died.<br /> <br /> The survivors largely have no idea what the fuck happened and have noticed their powers have changed.<br /> <br /> The campaign had the theme of, &quot;God's vengeance didn't even bother to kill you. You were that unimportant. The world ended for vampires not with a bang but a whimper. Now what?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-20T14:03:46-08:00","id":1546211,"title":"","content":"So how did that work out in your game CTPhipps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T09:47:27-08:00","id":1546247,"title":"","content":"The sects merging would really... not happened in my book. Parts of them can shuffle of course, but them uniting as a whole feels really really comic-book and gamey. If Blood Gods came, they would hide in their hidey holes, run towards crusade or bow as low as they could hoping for the best, each on their own. <br /> <br /> What I do like on the idea, is that in the Week of Nightmares more than one ANtediluvian makes a showoff. That I find interesting. <br /> Though Saulot and Cappadocius would be my choice for the momentous events, besides Brujah clawing from Carthage. Malk maybe too. <br /> <br /> Ventrue for me should never appear. If they were ever to appear, it would be to tell that the entire Anglo-Saxon Ventrue are doing stupid and failing their people, and not sparing the rod. Much less going king christ on earth laying down laws to every living creature, which is a power-up rubdown the Ventrue don't need (the authors already do that every single time they can; it's like corporates demand that they make the corporate clan the most best better cool awesome always). Besides, they should've been dead outside the walls of the second city. Leaving a mystery as to how descendants claimmed to be Embraced by them after that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Week of Nightmares is like the big boom that jumpstarts, like an Olympic opening cerimony, the entire Gehenna. <br /> But nothing is more Personal Horror than it being silent, quiet, slow, fading. With then some sudden burst here and there (like the Beckoning). Then falling sillent again. That is true terror. Not continuous bombardment. <br /> The Gothic-Punk needs the opportunity, shake-up and unconformity of the Punk, and the god-fearing conservative oppression of the Gothic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T13:36:15-08:00","id":1546256,"title":"","content":"Certainly we have that with elders and ancients who have been Beckoned for unknown reasons &amp; the ones do return are either more powerful or considerably weaker then before. It makes for some good tension as to what is happening in there world right now in our game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-26T18:06:53-08:00","id":1546437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546020-alternative-week-of-nightmares#post1546020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've found a neat alternative Week of nightmares on another forum where instead of Ravnos three other Three Antediluvians awaken, Brujah, Ventrue, and Lasombra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> TL;DR It starts with Ventrue standing in front of Palazzo Montecitorio in Rome declearing him self the king of kings and ends with all three of the Antediluvians committing a mutual kill or at least slnking off into shadows and the The Sabbat, the Anarchs, and the Camarilla getting forming a allance. Partly due to wanting to recover the devastation such the event and partly because Ventrue put a geass on all the vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honstly besides making for a good contrast of By nights studio version of WtA (and by extension WtE) where the garou nation split due to political differences. It make you think about other alternative Week of Nightmares where other Antediluvians awaken...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just out of curiosity, where does this power stem from? I mean I don't remember coming accross it (and I have at this point basically read every single book of the setting at this point).<br /> <br /> This version of the &quot;Week of Nightmares&quot; sounds interesting, especially comparing to the one we had, with one if not the least interesting Antediluvian coming only to be destroyed (I remember a friend of mine who said Justin did that because he didn't like the Ravnos clan lol). I just don't quite understand how could they get rid of Ventrue Lasombra and Brujah in a week tbh, but the rest of the idea is at the very least on the same level of the one we had, likely better. I'm curious about the source of the power, nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}